ody length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.20933333,"explanation":"DualShock 2 controller: 0.157 m (reference controller width). European badger: 0.75 m (reference head-and-body length). Ratio: 0.21×.\nA 15.7 cm controller-body width reference, excluding the cable.\nA 75 cm adult reference, excluding the tail. Adults vary in size.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DualShock","https://www.woodlandtrust.org.uk/trees-woods-and-wildlife/animals/mammals/badger/","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PlayStation2-DualShock2.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Animals_png_set_by_mossi889-d4uye4q_-_Badger.png"]}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs(game,slot,version,questions) VALUES('how-much-ish',10,7,'[{"id":"photo-size-v7-151","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the rolls-royce phantom iii to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Rolls-Royce Phantom III","dimension":"reference coachwork length","shape":"photo:rolls-royce"},"reference":{"name":"F tuba","dimension":"reference standing height","shape":"photo:tuba","measure":"90 cm · reference standing height"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":6.43333333,"explanation":"Rolls-Royce Phantom III: 5.79 m (reference coachwork length). F tuba: 0.9 m (reference standing height). Ratio: 6.43×.\nA 5.79 m coachwork reference; bodies were made by different coachbuilders.\nA 90 cm standing-height reference. Tubas vary substantially by pitch and design.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolls-Royce_Phantom_III","https://www.yamaha.com/en/musical_instrument_guide/tuba/structure/","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rolls_Royce_Phantom_III_1936_transparent.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Viennese_six-valve_bass_tuba_in_F(made_by_Jungwirth)_Transparent.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-152","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the kick scooter to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Kick scooter","dimension":"reference handlebar height","shape":"photo:skateboard"},"reference":{"name":"Computer mouse","dimension":"reference body length","shape":"photo:sega-mouse","measure":"11 cm · reference body length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":9.09090909,"explanation":"Kick scooter: 1 m (reference handlebar height). Computer mouse: 0.11 m (reference body length). Ratio: 9.09×.\nA one-metre handlebar-height reference. Adjustable scooters can be set lower.\nAn 11 cm computer-mouse body reference; the cable is excluded.","sources":["https://www.stigasports.com/","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sega-Dreamcast-Mouse-BR.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stiga_Route_200_S.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sega-Dreamcast-Mouse-BR.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-153","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the concert flute to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Concert flute","dimension":"typical assembled length","shape":"photo:flute"},"reference":{"name":"Concrete mixer truck","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:cement-truck","measure":"9 m · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.07444444,"explanation":"Concert flute: 0.67 m (typical assembled length). Concrete mixer truck: 9 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 0.07×.\nA reference concert flute about 67 cm long; model and footjoint affect length.\nA nine-metre mixer-truck reference. Chassis and mixer configuration affect exact length.","sources":["https://www.yamaha.com/en/musical_instrument_guide/flute/structure/","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_cement_mixer_truck.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yamaha_Flute_YFL-874W.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_cement_mixer_truck.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-154","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the city transit bus to match its real size.","target":{"name":"City transit bus","dimension":"40-foot bus length","shape":"photo:bus"},"reference":{"name":"Full-size electric guitar","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:guitar","measure":"1 m · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":12.2,"explanation":"City transit bus: 12.2 m (40-foot bus length). Full-size electric guitar: 1 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 12.20×.\nA nominal 40-foot (12.2 m) transit-bus reference; bumpers and model year affect exact length.\nA one-metre reference guitar. Overall length varies by model; this is not its string scale length.","sources":["https://www.gillig.com/low-floor","https://www.fender.com/articles/instruments/what-is-scale-length","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Transparent_Santa_Cruz_Metro_bus_0222.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guitar_3.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-155","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the open umbrella to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Open umbrella","dimension":"reference canopy width","shape":"photo:umbrella"},"reference":{"name":"Land tortoise","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:tortoise","measure":"30 cm · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":3.33333333,"explanation":"Open umbrella: 1 m (reference canopy width). Land tortoise: 0.3 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 3.33×.\nA one-metre canopy-width reference. Umbrella models vary.\nA 30 cm overall-length reference including the head and legs. Species and poses vary.","sources":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Umbrella.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Animals_png_set_by_mossi889-d4uye4q_-_Tortoise.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Umbrella.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Animals_png_set_by_mossi889-d4uye4q_-_Tortoise.png"]}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs(game,slot,version,questions) VALUES('how-much-ish',11,7,'[{"id":"photo-size-v7-156","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the nikon d90 to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Nikon D90","dimension":"camera body width","shape":"photo:nikon-d90"},"reference":{"name":"Broccoli head","dimension":"reference overall height","shape":"photo:broccoli","measure":"20 cm · reference overall height"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.66,"explanation":"Nikon D90: 0.132 m (camera body width). Broccoli head: 0.2 m (reference overall height). Ratio: 0.66×.\nD90 body width: 132 mm. Lens and strap are not part of the width measurement.\nA 20 cm broccoli reference including its stalk.","sources":["https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2008/0827_d90_01/","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Broccoli.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nikon_D90.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Broccoli.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-157","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the peacock butterfly to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Peacock butterfly","dimension":"reference wingspan","shape":"photo:peacock-butterfly"},"reference":{"name":"Wire stripper","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:wire-stripper","measure":"17 cm · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.38235294,"explanation":"Peacock butterfly: 0.065 m (reference wingspan). Wire stripper: 0.17 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 0.38×.\nA 65 mm wingspan reference with the wings spread.\nA 17 cm hand-tool reference. The photograph supplies the outline, not a scale calibration.","sources":["https://butterfly-conservation.org/butterflies/peacock","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wire_stripper.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aglais_io_-_3150.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wire_stripper.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-158","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the apple to match its real size.","ta