e body length","shape":"photo:sega-mouse"},"reference":{"name":"Land tortoise","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:tortoise","measure":"30 cm · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.36666667,"explanation":"Computer mouse: 0.11 m (reference body length). Land tortoise: 0.3 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 0.37×.\nAn 11 cm computer-mouse body reference; the cable is excluded.\nA 30 cm overall-length reference including the head and legs. Species and poses vary.","sources":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sega-Dreamcast-Mouse-BR.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Animals_png_set_by_mossi889-d4uye4q_-_Tortoise.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sega-Dreamcast-Mouse-BR.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Animals_png_set_by_mossi889-d4uye4q_-_Tortoise.png"]}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs(game,slot,version,questions) VALUES('how-much-ish',58,7,'[{"id":"photo-size-v7-391","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the dualshock 2 controller to match its real size.","target":{"name":"DualShock 2 controller","dimension":"reference controller width","shape":"photo:controller"},"reference":{"name":"Ledlenser T7M flashlight","dimension":"overall length","shape":"photo:flashlight","measure":"13.1 cm · overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":1.19847328,"explanation":"DualShock 2 controller: 0.157 m (reference controller width). Ledlenser T7M flashlight: 0.131 m (overall length). Ratio: 1.20×.\nA 15.7 cm controller-body width reference, excluding the cable.\nT7M overall length: 131 mm.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DualShock","https://www.ledlenser.my/product/flashlights/t7m/","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PlayStation2-DualShock2.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LED_LENSER_T7M_LED_flashlight.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-392","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the rolls-royce phantom iii to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Rolls-Royce Phantom III","dimension":"reference coachwork length","shape":"photo:rolls-royce"},"reference":{"name":"European badger","dimension":"reference head-and-body length","shape":"photo:badger","measure":"75 cm · reference head-and-body length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":7.72,"explanation":"Rolls-Royce Phantom III: 5.79 m (reference coachwork length). European badger: 0.75 m (reference head-and-body length). Ratio: 7.72×.\nA 5.79 m coachwork reference; bodies were made by different coachbuilders.\nA 75 cm adult reference, excluding the tail. Adults vary in size.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolls-Royce_Phantom_III","https://www.woodlandtrust.org.uk/trees-woods-and-wildlife/animals/mammals/badger/","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rolls_Royce_Phantom_III_1936_transparent.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Animals_png_set_by_mossi889-d4uye4q_-_Badger.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-393","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the concert flute to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Concert flute","dimension":"typical assembled length","shape":"photo:flute"},"reference":{"name":"City transit bus","dimension":"40-foot bus length","shape":"photo:bus","measure":"12.2 m · 40-foot bus length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.05491803,"explanation":"Concert flute: 0.67 m (typical assembled length). City transit bus: 12.2 m (40-foot bus length). Ratio: 0.05×.\nA reference concert flute about 67 cm long; model and footjoint affect length.\nA nominal 40-foot (12.2 m) transit-bus reference; bumpers and model year affect exact length.","sources":["https://www.yamaha.com/en/musical_instrument_guide/flute/structure/","https://www.gillig.com/low-floor","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yamaha_Flute_YFL-874W.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Transparent_Santa_Cruz_Metro_bus_0222.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-394","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the apple to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Apple","dimension":"reference fruit width","shape":"photo:apple"},"reference":{"name":"Disposable razor","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:razor","measure":"10 cm · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.8,"explanation":"Apple: 0.08 m (reference fruit width). Disposable razor: 0.1 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 0.80×.\nAn 8 cm wide reference apple; real apples vary by cultivar and growing conditions.\nA 10 cm razor reference, measured end to end.","sources":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Apple_in_lightbox.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Razor.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Apple_in_lightbox.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Razor.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-395","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the chameleon to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Chameleon","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:chameleon"},"reference":{"name":"Sony a5000","dimension":"camera body width","shape":"photo:sony-camera","measure":"10.96 cm · camera body width"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":2.73722628,"explanation":"Chameleon: 0.3 m (reference overall length). Sony a5000: 0.1096 m (camera body width). Ratio: 2.74×.\nA 30 cm reference specimen including the tail. Chameleon species vary widely.\nSony a5000 body width: 109.6 mm.","sources":["https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/chameleon","https://www.sony.com/electronics/interchangeable-lens-cameras/ilce-5000-kit/specifications","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ChameleonCutOut.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sony_A5000_white.png"]}]'::jsonb);
