erence standing height","shape":"photo:tuba"},"reference":{"name":"Atari Portfolio","dimension":"computer width","shape":"photo:calculator","measure":"20 cm · computer width"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":4.5,"explanation":"F tuba: 0.9 m (reference standing height). Atari Portfolio: 0.2 m (computer width). Ratio: 4.50×.\nA 90 cm standing-height reference. Tubas vary substantially by pitch and design.\nThe pocket computer is about 20 cm wide.","sources":["https://www.yamaha.com/en/musical_instrument_guide/tuba/structure/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atari_Portfolio","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Viennese_six-valve_bass_tuba_in_F(made_by_Jungwirth)_Transparent.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atari-Portfolio-Computer.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-554","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the broccoli head to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Broccoli head","dimension":"reference overall height","shape":"photo:broccoli"},"reference":{"name":"Game Boy Advance SP","dimension":"console width","shape":"photo:gba-sp","measure":"8.46 cm · console width"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":2.36406619,"explanation":"Broccoli head: 0.2 m (reference overall height). Game Boy Advance SP: 0.0846 m (console width). Ratio: 2.36×.\nA 20 cm broccoli reference including its stalk.\nThe SP is 84.6 mm wide, whether open or closed.","sources":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Broccoli.png","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Game_Boy_Advance_SP","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Broccoli.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Game-Boy-Advance-SP-Mk2.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-555","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the xd-picture card to match its real size.","target":{"name":"xD-Picture Card","dimension":"card width","shape":"photo:xd-card"},"reference":{"name":"Sunglasses","dimension":"reference front width","shape":"photo:sunglasses","measure":"14 cm · reference front width"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.17857143,"explanation":"xD-Picture Card: 0.025 m (card width). Sunglasses: 0.14 m (reference front width). Ratio: 0.18×.\nThe memory card is 25 mm wide and 20 mm high.\nA 14 cm front-width reference, not the length of the folding arms.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XD-Picture_Card","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sunglasses-1_retouch.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:XD_card_16M_Fujifilm_front.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sunglasses-1_retouch.png"]}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs(game,slot,version,questions) VALUES('how-much-ish',91,7,'[{"id":"photo-size-v7-556","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the sega nomad to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Sega Nomad","dimension":"console width","shape":"photo:sega-nomad"},"reference":{"name":"Full-size electric guitar","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:guitar","measure":"1 m · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.185,"explanation":"Sega Nomad: 0.185 m (console width). Full-size electric guitar: 1 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 0.18×.\nThe Nomad is approximately 18.5 cm wide.\nA one-metre reference guitar. Overall length varies by model; this is not its string scale length.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genesis_Nomad","https://www.fender.com/articles/instruments/what-is-scale-length","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sega-Nomad-Front_(rotated).png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guitar_3.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-557","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the apple to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Apple","dimension":"reference fruit width","shape":"photo:apple"},"reference":{"name":"Media remote control","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:remote","measure":"14.5 cm · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.55172414,"explanation":"Apple: 0.08 m (reference fruit width). Media remote control: 0.145 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 0.55×.\nAn 8 cm wide reference apple; real apples vary by cultivar and growing conditions.\nA 14.5 cm reference remote, measured end to end.","sources":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Apple_in_lightbox.png","https://www.playstation.com/en-us/accessories/media-remote/","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Apple_in_lightbox.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PlayStation_5_Media_Remote_-_front.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-558","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize 