DualShock 2 controller: 0.157 m (reference controller width). Ratio: 5.73×.\nA 90 cm standing-height reference. Tubas vary substantially by pitch and design.\nA 15.7 cm controller-body width reference, excluding the cable.","sources":["https://www.yamaha.com/en/musical_instrument_guide/tuba/structure/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DualShock","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Viennese_six-valve_bass_tuba_in_F(made_by_Jungwirth)_Transparent.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PlayStation2-DualShock2.png"]}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs(game,slot,version,questions) VALUES('how-much-ish',97,7,'[{"id":"photo-size-v7-586","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the full-size electric guitar to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Full-size electric guitar","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:guitar"},"reference":{"name":"Media remote control","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:remote","measure":"14.5 cm · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":6.89655172,"explanation":"Full-size electric guitar: 1 m (reference overall length). Media remote control: 0.145 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 6.90×.\nA one-metre reference guitar. Overall length varies by model; this is not its string scale length.\nA 14.5 cm reference remote, measured end to end.","sources":["https://www.fender.com/articles/instruments/what-is-scale-length","https://www.playstation.com/en-us/accessories/media-remote/","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guitar_3.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PlayStation_5_Media_Remote_-_front.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-587","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the size-7 basketball to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Size-7 basketball","dimension":"nominal diameter","shape":"photo:basketball"},"reference":{"name":"Nikon D90","dimension":"camera body width","shape":"photo:nikon-d90","measure":"13.2 cm · camera body width"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":1.81060606,"explanation":"Size-7 basketball: 0.239 m (nominal diameter). Nikon D90: 0.132 m (camera body width). Ratio: 1.81×.\nA nominal diameter of 23.9 cm, corresponding to about 75 cm circumference.\nD90 body width: 132 mm. Lens and strap are not part of the width measurement.","sources":["https://www.fiba.basketball/en/official-basketball-rules","https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2008/0827_d90_01/","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Isolated_basketball.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nikon_D90.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-588","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the small scissors to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Small scissors","dimension":"reference end-to-end length","shape":"photo:scissors"},"reference":{"name":"2010 Mac mini","dimension":"enclosure width","shape":"photo:mac-mini","measure":"19.7 cm · enclosure width"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.7106599,"explanation":"Small scissors: 0.14 m (reference end-to-end length). 2010 Mac mini: 0.197 m (enclosure width). Ratio: 0.71×.\nA 14 cm household-scissors reference, measured from handle end to blade tip.\nThis Mac mini generation has a 19.7 cm square footprint.","sources":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Small_pair_of_blue_scissors.png","https://support.apple.com/en-us/112588","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Small_pair_of_blue_scissors.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mac_mini_server.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-589","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the original nintendo ds to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Original Nintendo DS","dimension":"console width","shape":"photo:nintendo-ds"},"reference":{"name":"Disposable razor","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:razor","measure":"10 cm · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":1.487,"explanation":"Original Nintendo DS: 0.1487 m (console width). Disposable razor: 0.1 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 1.49×.\nOriginal DS width: 148.7 mm.\nA 10 cm razor reference, measured end to end.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nintendo_DS","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Razor.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nintendo-DS-Fat-Blue.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Razor.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-590","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the three-cup moka pot to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Three-cup moka pot","dimension":"reference height","shape":"photo:coffee-pot"},"reference":{"name":"Nintendo Switch","dimension":"width with Joy-Con","shape":"photo:switch","measure":"23.9 cm · width with Joy-Con"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.66945607,"explanation":"Three-cup moka pot: 0.16 m (reference height). Nintendo Switch: 0.239 m (width with Joy-Con). Ratio: 0.67×.\nA roughly 16 cm three-cup reference. Moka pots are sold in many capacities.\nOriginal Nintendo Switch: 239 mm wide with Joy-Con attached.","sources":["https://www.bialetti.com/ee_en/moka-express.html","https://www.nintendo.com/us/gaming-systems/switch/tech-specs/","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moka_Express_sideview.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nintendo-Switch-wJoyCons-BlRd-Standing-FL.png"]}]'::jsonb);
