:"5 m · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.18,"explanation":"F tuba: 0.9 m (reference standing height). Road roller: 5 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 0.18×.\nA 90 cm standing-height reference. Tubas vary substantially by pitch and design.\nA five-metre road-roller reference; construction machines come in many sizes.","sources":["https://www.yamaha.com/en/musical_instrument_guide/tuba/structure/","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Road_roller.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Viennese_six-valve_bass_tuba_in_F(made_by_Jungwirth)_Transparent.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Road_roller.png"]}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs(game,slot,version,questions) VALUES('how-much-ish',107,7,'[{"id":"photo-size-v7-636","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the european badger to match its real size.","target":{"name":"European badger","dimension":"reference head-and-body length","shape":"photo:badger"},"reference":{"name":"Rolls-Royce Phantom III","dimension":"reference coachwork length","shape":"photo:rolls-royce","measure":"5.79 m · reference coachwork length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.12953368,"explanation":"European badger: 0.75 m (reference head-and-body length). Rolls-Royce Phantom III: 5.79 m (reference coachwork length). Ratio: 0.13×.\nA 75 cm adult reference, excluding the tail. Adults vary in size.\nA 5.79 m coachwork reference; bodies were made by different coachbuilders.","sources":["https://www.woodlandtrust.org.uk/trees-woods-and-wildlife/animals/mammals/badger/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolls-Royce_Phantom_III","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Animals_png_set_by_mossi889-d4uye4q_-_Badger.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rolls_Royce_Phantom_III_1936_transparent.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-637","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the sunglasses to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Sunglasses","dimension":"reference front width","shape":"photo:sunglasses"},"reference":{"name":"Commodore 128","dimension":"keyboard-computer width","shape":"photo:keyboard","measure":"43 cm · keyboard-computer width"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.3255814,"explanation":"Sunglasses: 0.14 m (reference front width). Commodore 128: 0.43 m (keyboard-computer width). Ratio: 0.33×.\nA 14 cm front-width reference, not the length of the folding arms.\nA 43 cm wide keyboard-computer reference.","sources":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sunglasses-1_retouch.png","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commodore_128","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sunglasses-1_retouch.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Commodore-128.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-638","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the game boy advance to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Game Boy Advance","dimension":"console width","shape":"photo:gba"},"reference":{"name":"Kick scooter","dimension":"reference handlebar height","shape":"photo:skateboard","measure":"1 m · reference handlebar height"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.1445,"explanation":"Game Boy Advance: 0.1445 m (console width). Kick scooter: 1 m (reference handlebar height). Ratio: 0.14×.\nOriginal model: 144.5 mm wide; cartridges are excluded from the width.\nA one-metre handlebar-height reference. Adjustable scooters can be set lower.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Game_Boy_Advance","https://www.stigasports.com/","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GameBoyAdvance-transparent.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stiga_Route_200_S.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-639","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the game boy advance sp to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Game Boy Advance SP","dimension":"console width","shape":"photo:gba-sp"},"reference":{"name":"Full-size electric guitar","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:guitar","measure":"1 m · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.0846,"explanation":"Game Boy Advance SP: 0.0846 m (console width). Full-size electric guitar: 1 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 0.08×.\nThe SP is 84.6 mm wide, whether open or closed.\nA one-metre reference guitar. Overall length varies by model; this is not its string scale length.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Game_Boy_Advance_SP","https://www.fender.com/articles/instruments/what-is-scale-length","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Game-Boy-Advance-SP-Mk2.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guitar_3.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-640","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the open umbrella to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Open umbrella","dimension":"reference canopy width","shape":"photo:umbrella"},"reference":{"name":"Original Nintendo DS","dimension":"console width","shape":"photo:nintendo-ds","measure":"14.87 cm · console width"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":6.72494956,"explanation":"Open umbrella: 1 m (reference canopy width). Original Nintendo DS: 0.1487 m (console width). Ratio: 6.72×.\nA one-metre canopy-width reference. Umbrella models vary.\nOriginal DS width: 148.7 mm.","sources":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Umbrella.png","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nintendo_DS","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Umbrella.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nintendo-DS-Fat-Blue.png"]}]'::jsonb);
