name":"Atari Portfolio","dimension":"computer width","shape":"photo:calculator"},"reference":{"name":"Size-7 basketball","dimension":"nominal diameter","shape":"photo:basketball","measure":"23.9 cm · nominal diameter"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.83682008,"explanation":"Atari Portfolio: 0.2 m (computer width). Size-7 basketball: 0.239 m (nominal diameter). Ratio: 0.84×.\nThe pocket computer is about 20 cm wide.\nA nominal diameter of 23.9 cm, corresponding to about 75 cm circumference.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atari_Portfolio","https://www.fiba.basketball/en/official-basketball-rules","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atari-Portfolio-Computer.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Isolated_basketball.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-644","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the nintendo switch to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Nintendo Switch","dimension":"width with Joy-Con","shape":"photo:switch"},"reference":{"name":"Full-size violin","dimension":"typical overall length","shape":"photo:violin","measure":"59 cm · typical overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.40508475,"explanation":"Nintendo Switch: 0.239 m (width with Joy-Con). Full-size violin: 0.59 m (typical overall length). Ratio: 0.41×.\nOriginal Nintendo Switch: 239 mm wide with Joy-Con attached.\nA full-size violin is about 59 cm overall. The bow is excluded.","sources":["https://www.nintendo.com/us/gaming-systems/switch/tech-specs/","https://www.yamaha.com/en/musical_instrument_guide/violin/structure/","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nintendo-Switch-wJoyCons-BlRd-Standing-FL.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Violin_VL100_(cropped).png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-645","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the chameleon to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Chameleon","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:chameleon"},"reference":{"name":"Olympus E-PL1","dimension":"camera body width","shape":"photo:olympus","mea