ence long-axis length","shape":"photo:coffee-bean","measure":"1 cm · reference long-axis length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":8.46,"explanation":"Game Boy Advance SP: 0.0846 m (console width). Coffee bean: 0.01 m (reference long-axis length). Ratio: 8.46×.\nThe SP is 84.6 mm wide, whether open or closed.\nA 10 mm roasted-coffee-bean reference.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Game_Boy_Advance_SP","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coffee_bean_transparent.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Game-Boy-Advance-SP-Mk2.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coffee_bean_transparent.png"]}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs(game,slot,version,questions) VALUES('how-much-ish',129,7,'[{"id":"photo-size-v7-746","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the honda s2000 to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Honda S2000","dimension":"vehicle length","shape":"photo:honda-s2000"},"reference":{"name":"Open umbrella","dimension":"reference canopy width","shape":"photo:umbrella","measure":"1 m · reference canopy width"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":4.135,"explanation":"Honda S2000: 4.135 m (vehicle length). Open umbrella: 1 m (reference canopy width). Ratio: 4.13×.\n2005 S2000 overall length: 4.135 m.\nA one-metre canopy-width reference. Umbrella models vary.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honda_S2000","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Umbrella.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HondaS2000-004.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Umbrella.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-747","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the plains zebra to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Plains zebra","dimension":"reference head-and-body length","shape":"photo:zebra"},"reference":{"name":"Atari Portfolio","dimension":"computer width","shape":"photo:calculator","measure":"20 cm · computer width"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":12,"explanation":"Plains zebra: 2.4 m (reference head-and-body length). Atari Portfolio: 0.2 m (computer width). Ratio: 12.00×.\nA 2.4 m head-and-body reference; the tail is not part of this measurement.\nThe pocket computer is about 20 cm wide.","sources":["https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/zebra","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atari_Portfolio","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Animals_png_set_by_mossi889-d4uye4q_-_Zebra.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atari-Portfolio-Computer.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-748","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the road roller to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Road roller","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:road-roller"},"reference":{"name":"Chameleon","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:chameleon","measure":"30 cm · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":16.66666667,"explanation":"Road roller: 5 m (reference overall length). Chameleon: 0.3 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 16.67×.\nA five-metre road-roller reference; construction machines come in many sizes.\nA 30 cm reference specimen including the tail. Chameleon species vary widely.","sources":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Road_roller.png","https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/chameleon","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Road_roller.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ChameleonCutOut.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-749","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the rolls-royce phantom iii to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Rolls-Royce Phantom III","dimension":"reference coachwork length","shape":"photo:rolls-royce"},"reference":{"name":"Kick scooter","dimension":"reference handlebar height","shape":"photo:skateboard","measure":"1 m · reference handlebar height"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":5.79,"explanation":"Rolls-Royce Phantom III: 5.79 m (reference coachwork length). Kick scooter: 1 m (reference handlebar height). Ratio: 5.79×.\nA 5.79 m coachwork reference; bodies were made by different coachbuilders.\nA one-metre handlebar-height reference. Adjustable scooters can be set lower.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolls-Royce_Phantom_III","https://www.stigasports.com/","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rolls_Royce_Phantom_III_1936_transparent.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stiga_Route_200_S.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-750","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the climbing hammer to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Climbing hammer","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:climbing-hammer"},"reference":{"name":"BlackBerry Q10","dimension":"phone height","shape":"photo:blackberry","measure":"11.96 cm · phone height"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":2.5083612,"explanation":"Climbing hammer: 0.3 m (reference overall length). BlackBerry Q10: 0.1196 m (phone height). Ratio: 2.51×.\nA 30 cm hand-tool reference.\nBlackBerry Q10 height: 119.6 mm.","sources":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Climbing_hammer.png","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BlackBerry_Q10","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Climbing_hammer.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blackberry-Q10-transparent.png"]}]'::jsonb);
