ube width"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":1,"explanation":"xD-Picture Card: 0.025 m (card width). Billiard chalk cube: 0.025 m (reference cube width). Ratio: 1.00×.\nThe memory card is 25 mm wide and 20 mm high.\nA 2.5 cm chalk-cube reference.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XD-Picture_Card","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Billiard_chalk_20050724.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:XD_card_16M_Fujifilm_front.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Billiard_chalk_20050724.png"]}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs(game,slot,version,questions) VALUES('how-much-ish',161,7,'[{"id":"photo-size-v7-906","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the size-7 basketball to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Size-7 basketball","dimension":"nominal diameter","shape":"photo:basketball"},"reference":{"name":"Wire stripper","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:wire-stripper","measure":"17 cm · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":1.40588235,"explanation":"Size-7 basketball: 0.239 m (nominal diameter). Wire stripper: 0.17 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 1.41×.\nA nominal diameter of 23.9 cm, corresponding to about 75 cm circumference.\nA 17 cm hand-tool reference. The photograph supplies the outline, not a scale calibration.","sources":["https://www.fiba.basketball/en/official-basketball-rules","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wire_stripper.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Isolated_basketball.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wire_stripper.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-907","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the avocado to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Avocado","dimension":"reference fruit length","shape":"photo:avocado"},"reference":{"name":"Three-cup moka pot","dimension":"reference height","shape":"photo:coffee-pot","measure":"16 cm · reference height"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.875,"explanation":"Avocado: 0.14 m (reference fruit length). Three-cup moka pot: 0.16 m (reference height). Ratio: 0.88×.\nA 14 cm reference avocado. Fruit sizes vary considerably.\nA roughly 16 cm three-cup reference. Moka pots are sold in many capacities.","sources":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Avocado.png","https://www.bialetti.com/ee_en/moka-express.html","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Avocado.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moka_Express_sideview.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-908","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the broccoli head to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Broccoli head","dimension":"reference overall height","shape":"photo:broccoli"},"reference":{"name":"Land tortoise","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:tortoise","measure":"30 cm · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.66666667,"explanation":"Broccoli head: 0.2 m (reference overall height). Land tortoise: 0.3 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 0.67×.\nA 20 cm broccoli reference including its stalk.\nA 30 cm overall-length reference including the head and legs. Species and poses vary.","sources":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Broccoli.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Animals_png_set_by_mossi889-d4uye4q_-_Tortoise.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Broccoli.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Animals_png_set_by_mossi889-d4uye4q_-_Tortoise.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-909","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the tennis ball to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Tennis ball","dimension":"reference ball diameter","shape":"photo:tennis-ball"},"reference":{"name":"Seven-spot ladybird","dimension":"reference body length","shape":"photo:ladybird","measure":"0.7 cm · reference body length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":9.57142857,"explanation":"Tennis ball: 0.067 m (reference ball diameter). Seven-spot ladybird: 0.007 m (reference body length). Ratio: 9.57×.\nA 6.7 cm diameter reference, within the standard ball-size range.\nA 7 mm adult reference, excluding legs and antennae.","sources":["https://www.itftennis.com/en/about-us/tennis-tech/approved-balls/","https://www.wildlifetrusts.org/wildlife-explorer/invertebrates/beetles/7-spot-ladybird","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tennisball2.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coccinella-septempunctata--Trp-1.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-910","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the sewing needle to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Sewing needle","dimension":"reference end-to-end length","shape":"photo:needle"},"reference":{"name":"Bicycle master-link pliers","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:pliers","measure":"17 cm · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.23529412,"explanation":"Sewing needle: 0.04 m (reference end-to-end length). Bicycle master-link pliers: 0.17 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 0.24×.\nA 4 cm reference needle. Sewing needles come in multiple lengths.\nA 17 cm pliers reference; tool models differ.","sources":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sewing_needle.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Master_link_pliers.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sewing_needle.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Master_link_pliers.png"]}]'::jsonb);
