ameleon","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:chameleon"},"reference":{"name":"NES controller","dimension":"body width","shape":"photo:nes-controller","measure":"12.3 cm · body width"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":2.43902439,"explanation":"Chameleon: 0.3 m (reference overall length). NES controller: 0.123 m (body width). Ratio: 2.44×.\nA 30 cm reference specimen including the tail. Chameleon species vary widely.\nA 123 mm controller body reference; the cable is excluded.","sources":["https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/chameleon","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nintendo_Entertainment_System","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ChameleonCutOut.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nintendo-Entertainment-System-NES-Controller-FL.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-979","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the atari portfolio to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Atari Portfolio","dimension":"computer width","shape":"photo:calculator"},"reference":{"name":"Drywall screw","dimension":"reference screw length","shape":"photo:screw","measure":"3.5 cm · reference screw length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":5.71428571,"explanation":"Atari Portfolio: 0.2 m (computer width). Drywall screw: 0.035 m (reference screw length). Ratio: 5.71×.\nThe pocket computer is about 20 cm wide.\nA 35 mm drywall-screw reference; this is one selected size, not a universal screw length.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atari_Portfolio","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Drywall_screw.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atari-Portfolio-Computer.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Drywall_screw.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-980","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the akg c214 microphone to match its real size.","target":{"name":"AKG C214 microphone","dimension":"microphone height","shape":"photo:akg-microphone"},"reference":{"name":"Wire stripper","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:wire-stripper","measure":"17 cm · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.94117647,"explanation":"AKG C214 microphone: 0.16 m (microphone height). Wire stripper: 0.17 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 0.94×.\nC214 microphone height: 160 mm, without a stand.\nA 17 cm hand-tool reference. The photograph supplies the outline, not a scale calibration.","sources":["https://www.akg.com/Microphones/Condenser%20Microphones/C214.html","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wire_stripper.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AKG_C214_Condenser_microphone.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wire_stripper.png"]}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs(game,slot,version,questions) VALUES('how-much-ish',176,7,'[{"id":"photo-size-v7-981","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the concert flute to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Concert flute","dimension":"typical assembled length","shape":"photo:flute"},"reference":{"name":"Olympus E-PL1","dimension":"camera body width","shape":"photo:olympus","measure":"11.46 cm · camera body width"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":5.84642234,"explanation":"Concert flute: 0.67 m (typical assembled length). Olympus E-PL1: 0.1146 m (camera body width). Ratio: 5.85×.\nA reference concert flute about 67 cm long; model and footjoint affect length.\nE-PL1 body width: 114.6 mm.","sources":["https://www.yamaha.com/en/musical_instrument_guide/flute/structure/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olympus_PEN_E-PL1","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yamaha_Flute_YFL-874W.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Olympus_E-PL1.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-982","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the disposable razor to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Disposable razor","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:razor"},"reference":{"name":"xD-Picture Card","dimension":"card width","shape":"photo:xd-card","measure":"2.5 cm · card width"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":4,"explanation":"Disposable razor: 0.1 m (reference overall length). xD-Picture Card: 0.025 m (card width). Ratio: 4.00×.\nA 10 cm razor reference, measured end to end.\nThe memory card is 25 mm wide and 20 mm high.","sources":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Razor.png","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XD-Picture_Card","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Razor.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:XD_card_16M_Fujifilm_front.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-983","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the sewing needle to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Sewing needle","dimension":"reference end-to-end length","shape":"photo:needle"},"reference":{"name":"Media remote control","dimension":"reference overall length","shape":"photo:remote","measure":"14.5 cm · reference overall length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.27586207,"explanation":"Sewing needle: 0.04 m (reference end-to-end length). Media remote control: 0.145 m (reference overall length). Ratio: 0.28×.\nA 4 cm reference needle. Sewing needles come in multiple lengths.\nA 14.5 cm reference remote, measured end to end.","sources":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sewing_needle.png","https://www.playstation.com/en-us/accessories/media-remote/","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sewing_needle.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PlayStation_5_Media_Remote_-_front.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-984","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the avocado to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Avocado","dimension":"reference fruit length","shape":"photo:avocado"},"reference":{"name":"Dreamcast VMU","dimension":"unit height","shape":"photo:dreamcast-vmu","measure":"8 cm · unit height"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":1.75,"explanation":"Avocado: 0.14 m (reference fruit length). Dreamcast VMU: 0.08 m (unit height). Ratio: 1.75×.\nA 14 cm reference avocado. Fruit sizes vary considerably.\nThe Visual Memory Unit is about 80 mm high.","sources":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Avocado.png","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/VMU","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Avocado.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sega-Dreamcast-VMU.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-985","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the ledlenser t7m flashlight to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Ledlenser T7M flashlight","dimension":"overall length","shape":"photo:flashlight"},"reference":{"name":"Game Boy Micro","dimension":"console width","shape":"photo:gameboy-micro","measure":"10.1 cm · console width"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":1.2970297,"explanation":"Ledlenser T7M flashlight: 0.131 m (overall length). Game Boy Micro: 0.101 m (console width). Ratio: 1.30×.\nT7M overall length: 131 mm.\nThe Micro is 101 mm wide.","sources":["https://www.ledlenser.my/product/flashlights/t7m/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Game_Boy_Micro","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LED_LENSER_T7M_LED_flashlight.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Game-Boy-Micro.png"]}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs(game,slot,version,questions) VALUES('how-much-ish',177,7,'[{"id":"photo-size-v7-986","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the game boy advance to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Game Boy Advance","dimension":"console width","shape":"photo:gba"},"reference":{"name":"Soprano recorder","dimension":"reference length","shape":"photo:recorder","measure":"32 cm · reference length"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.4515625,"explanation":"Game Boy Advance: 0.1445 m (console width). Soprano recorder: 0.32 m (reference length). Ratio: 0.45×.\nOriginal model: 144.5 mm wide; cartridges are excluded from the width.\nA 32 cm soprano recorder reference; recorders come in many sizes.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Game_Boy_Advance","https://www.yamaha.com/en/musical_instrument_guide/recorder/structure/","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GameBoyAdvance-transparent.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yamaha_Soprano_Recorder_YRS-61.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-987","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the sunglasses to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Sunglasses","dimension":"reference front width","shape":"photo:sunglasses"},"reference":{"name":"Size-7 basketball","dimension":"nominal diameter","shape":"photo:basketball","measure":"23.9 cm · nominal diameter"},"bounds":[0.02,50],"answer":0.58577406,"explanation":"Sunglasses: 0.14 m (reference front width). Size-7 basketball: 0.239 m (nominal diameter). Ratio: 0.59×.\nA 14 cm front-width reference, not the length of the folding arms.\nA nominal diameter of 23.9 cm, corresponding to about 75 cm circumference.","sources":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sunglasses-1_retouch.png","https://www.fiba.basketball/en/official-basketball-rules","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sunglasses-1_retouch.png","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Isolated_basketball.png"]},{"id":"photo-size-v7-988","version":7,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resiz